rces></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-11180717-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>11180717</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="XP" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9161799-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9161799</doc-number><kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="WO-1999008964-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>WO</country><doc-number>1999008964</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1116692A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAI HIDEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOHO TITANIUM CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAWAKI TETSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOHO TITANIUM CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAWAKI, TETSUYA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAI HIDEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAWAKI TETSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAWAKI, TETSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for preparing lithium manganate having spinel structure which compsises contacting a manganese halide and lithium at a temperature of 100 DEG C or less in a liquid phase to react with each other; a lithium manganate which is prepared according to the method, is represented by the formula LixMnOy, wherein x represents a real number satisfying 0 &lt; x &lt;/= 0.8, y represents a real number satisfying 1.8 &lt;/= y &lt;/= 2.4, and has an average particle diameter of 1 to 50  mu m and a specific surface area of 10 to 15m&lt;2&gt;/g; a positive electrode for a lithium secondary cell comprising the lithium manganate as an active material; and a lithium secondary cell using the positive electrode.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un procédé de préparation de manganate de lithium présentant une structure de spinelle. Le procédé consiste en placer un halogénure de manganèse au contact du lithium, à une température d'au plus 100  DEG C dans une phase liquide, pour provoquer une réaction des deux éléments. On obtient un manganate de lithium de la formule LixMnOy, dans laquelle x est un nombre réel correspondant à 0 &lt; x &lt;/= 0,8; y est un nombre réel correspondant à 1,8 &lt;/= y &lt;/= 2,4 et présente un diamètre moyen des particules compris entre 1 et 50  mu m et une aire superficielle spécifique de 10 à 15 m&lt;2&gt;/g. L'invention porte en outre sur une électrode positive pour cellule secondaire au lithium contenant le manganate de lithium comme matière active, et sur une cellule secondaire au lithium utilisant ladite électrode positive.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>